        "id": "ex-jhs2ct-t13-1",
        "title": "Calculating Cost and Selling Price for a Wooden Coffee Table",
        "problem": "A student enterprise fabricates a wooden coffee table. The costs incurred are: Timber = GH₵ 220; Wood glue, screws, and sandpaper = GH₵ 40; Polyurethane varnish = GH₵ 50; Labor (10 hours at GH₵ 8/hr) = GH₵ 80; Workshop overheads and transport = GH₵ 30. If the enterprise targets a 25% profit margin, calculate (a) Total production cost, (b) Profit amount, and (c) Final selling price.",
        "stepByStepSolution": [
          "Step 1: Calculate Direct Material Cost: Timber (GH₵ 220) + Hardware/consumables (GH₵ 40) + Varnish (GH₵ 50) = GH₵ 310.",
          "Step 2: Calculate Direct Labor Cost: 10 hours × GH₵ 8/hr = GH₵ 80.",
          "Step 3: Calculate Total Production Cost: Direct Materials (GH₵ 310) + Direct Labor (GH₵ 80) + Overheads (GH₵ 30) = GH₵ 420.",
          "Step 4: Calculate Profit Markup (25%): Profit = Total Cost × 25% = GH₵ 420 × 0.25 = GH₵ 105.",
          "Step 5: Calculate Selling Price: Selling Price = Total Cost + Profit = GH₵ 420 + GH₵ 105 = GH₵ 525."
        ],
        "keyTakeaway": "Selling price must recover all direct materials, direct labor, and overheads, plus the targeted profit margin."
